  "body": {
    "id": "thm:ordinary-id-reduction",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "If \\(H=\\{s_{\\emptyset}\\}\\), every selector gate is laid back on \\(E_H\\), and \\(S\\) has no latent root shared with \\(V\\), then \\(G_H^N\\) is the ordinary semi-Markovian expansion on \\(V\\), \\(\\Phi_H\\) equals its ordinary observational-target relation, and \\(\\operatorname{SA\\mbox{-}CS\\mbox{-}ID}\\) reduces to the ID formula-or-hedge classification of Shpitser and Pearl.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "H",
      "sempty",
      "EH",
      "S",
      "V",
      "GN",
      "PhiH",
      "SACSID"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "ass:exact-selector-support",
      "thm:normalization-equivalence",
      "lem:ordinary-id-formula-or-hedge",
      "lem:ordinary-id-residual-compiler",
      "def:initial-token-compiler",
      "def:fixing-transition",
      "def:elimination-transition"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Because \\(H=\\{s_{\\emptyset}\\}\\), exact selector support gives\n\\[\np_\\theta(S=s_{\\emptyset})=1.\n\\tag{11}\n\\]\nEvery selector gate is laid back at this value, so its known multiplexer selects the natural response table.  Since \\(S\\) shares no latent root with \\(V\\), suppressing its deterministic coordinate removes neither a substantive latent parent nor any root-independence restriction.  Support-active normalization retains every natural response coordinate and substantive latent-root law.  Thus \\(G_H^N\\), after suppressing \\(S\\), is exactly the ordinary semi-Markovian expansion on \\(V\\).\n\nFor every substantive cell \\(v\\), (11) implies\n\\[\np_\\theta(V=v,S=s_{\\emptyset})=p_\\theta(V=v).\n\\tag{12}\n\\]\nThe intervention \\(S=s_{\\emptyset}\\) changes no laid-back gate, so \\(T_{a,H}\\) is the ordinary \\(\\operatorname{do}(A=a)\\) target.  Applying \\(\\textnormal{thm:normalization-equivalence}\\) to (12) proves equality of \\(\\Phi_H\\) and the ordinary observational--target relation.\n\nThere is no active selector occurrence, hence \\(\\Sigma=\\varnothing\\).  The splitter in \\(\\textnormal{def:initial-token-compiler}\\) now has exactly the ordinary recursive ID cases: removal of nonancestors, proper-district splitting, and reachable fixing.  Its reachability test is\n\\[\n\\operatorname{dis}_{D}(W)\\cap\\operatorname{de}_{D}(W)=\\{W\\},\n\\tag{13}\n\\]\nand the successor kernel is \\(K_D/\\sum_{x_W}K_D\\).  The elimination cases are the ordinary finite marginal and topologically ordered district factorization.  Therefore every nonresidual transition agrees algebraically with the corresponding ID step.\n\nAt an ordinary residual, \\(\\textnormal{lem:ordinary-id-residual-compiler}\\) completes the comparison.  A successful ID recursion is compiled to a verifier-accepted projection circuit.  A failed recursion returns a hedge and is compiled to a rational support-exact global-twin box with equal strictly positive observational laws and unequal targets.  By \\(\\textnormal{lem:ordinary-id-formula-or-hedge}\\), these two cases are exhaustive and coincide respectively with identification and nonidentification.  Thus SA-CS-ID reduces to the Shpitser--Pearl formula-or-hedge classification, while (11)--(12) prove the claimed equality of model semantics.",
    "justification": "The proved reduction shows that the support-aware compiler agrees with classical completeness when systematic selection disappears.",
    "gap": "The dedicated ordinary residual compiler removes any dependence of this sanity check on the still-open general selector residual theorem.",
    "consumer": "Implementers can regression-test formula outputs and strictly positive hedge-twin certificates against established ordinary ID cases.",
